closed forms A_m, B_m, C_m = 0 agree with the exact block sums (N = 3..9, all m, three latitudes, 40 digits): True
N = 2: stable at every latitude
N = 3: stable at every latitude
N = 4: stable iff cos^2(theta) >= 1/3,  i.e. kappa = cot(theta) >= sqrt(2)/2
N = 5: stable iff cos^2(theta) >= 1/2,  i.e. kappa = cot(theta) >= 1
N = 6: stable iff cos^2(theta) >= 4/5,  i.e. kappa = cot(theta) >= 2
N = 7: stable only at the pole
N = 8: never stable
